<td>
\verbinclude StructuredImpurity.out
</td></tr></table>

\subsection StructuredExampleDivideAndConquer The merge step of divide and conquer

Cuppen's method [25] tears a symmetric tridiagonal matrix into two halves plus a rank-one coupling; after the halves
are diagonalized, what remains is the diagonal-plus-rank-one eigenproblem that \ref DPR1EigenSolver solves from the
secular equation, with eigenvectors orthogonal to working accuracy by the construction of Gu and Eisenstat [9]. The
example performs one such merge and compares with \c SelfAdjointEigenSolver.

